course: dictionary
lesson: 3711
title: Flemish: a place, a people, a language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Flemish is a word with more than one job. As an adjective, it tells you something is to do with Flanders, the northern Dutch-speaking part of Belgium, or its people. In «Pieter Bruegel the Elder, a Flemish painter of the 1500s, painted busy village scenes», Flemish describes the painter, so Bruegel came from Flanders.
explain: Look at the words around Flemish to see which job it does. In «Flemish painter», it describes a person. On its own, as a noun, it names a language: the Dutch spoken in Belgium. Ask yourself: is it describing a person or thing, or naming a language?
explain: Context can also show you where a word is used. In a geography lesson about Belgium, you might read about Flemish-speaking, French-speaking and German-speaking areas. Each name tells you which language people use in that area.
fact: Flemish means to do with Flanders, the northern Dutch-speaking part of Belgium, or its people.
fact: Flemish is also the name for the Dutch spoken in Belgium.
fact: «Flemish art» means paintings by artists from Flanders, like Bruegel and Van Eyck.
fact: Belgium has Flemish-, French- and German-speaking areas.
fact: «Flemish painters» and «Flemish speakers» are phrases you will meet in history, art and geography lessons.
exercise: «Pieter Bruegel the Elder, a Flemish painter of the 1500s, painted busy village scenes.» What does Flemish describe here? | The village scenes | The year 1500 | *The painter, who came from Flanders | The picture puzzle
exercise: Belgium has Flemish-speaking, French-speaking and German-speaking areas. What does Flemish-speaking mean? | Where people paint pictures | *Where people speak Dutch | Where people speak German | Where people speak French
exercise: «She speaks Flemish at home.» What does Flemish mean here? | *The Dutch language spoken in Belgium | A type of busy village scene | A painting from the 1500s | A village in Flanders
test: «Flemish art» means paintings by which artists? | Artists from the French-speaking part of Belgium | Artists from Germany | Artists who only paint villages | *Artists from Flanders, like Bruegel and Van Eyck
test: Which word tells you a painter comes from Flanders? | Picture | Village | *Flemish | Busy
exam: What does Flemish mean in «The Flemish are proud of their painters»? | A type of painting | A kind of village scene | A French-speaking town in Belgium | *The people of Flanders, the northern Dutch-speaking part of Belgium
